# Feature: a local rate over a bare observable that never moves (issue #40).
# Tests:   the cost of the per-event rescan that issue #38 put behind a local
#          rate reading a global, at an instance count where that cost shows.
#          `Vol` is written bare inside `aflip`, so it is the system-wide
#          count and the rule is marked as tracking a global — but nothing in
#          the model touches V, so `Vol` is 50 at every event of the run and
#          not one of those rescans can change a single per-instance rate.
#          Skipping them is exact, and this model is where "exact" and
#          "free" have to coincide.
#
#          This is the shape the three corpora had no model of at all: a bare
#          observable inside a local function appears in none of their 199
#          XMLs, so nothing timed the path and a 20x regression sat in it
#          unseen (#39).  It is also the common shape — a bare observable is
#          typically a volume proxy, a total or a clock, and those are
#          constant or near-constant for most of a run.
#
# Oracle:  the same exact binomial death process ft_local_fcn_global_obs uses,
#          scaled up.  A(m~0,p~1) flips at kf*Vol*Aphos(x) = 2e-4*50*1 = 0.01;
#          A(m~0,p~0) has Aphos(x) = 0 and must never react, which is what
#          keeps the TAGGED half of the classification pinned while the bare
#          half is under test.  Nothing consumes V, so Vol stays 50:
#            Aoff(t) = 2000 + 20000*exp(-0.01 t)
#            Aoff(100) = 2000 + 20000*exp(-1) = 9357.6
#
# Tier:    stress (network-free; NFsim reference only).
# Target:  well under 1 s of RM wall time, and that target IS the assertion.
#          The other stress models are sized to run long; this one is sized so
#          that a rule which rescans unconditionally cannot run short.  22000
#          molecules match the rule's reactant pattern at t=0 and ~12800
#          events fire, so a per-event rescan is ~2e8 local-rate evaluations:
#          33 s against 0.16 s measured, i.e. a regression lands in perf_diff
#          as a ~200x column rather than as noise.  The correctness half is a
#          plain z-score against NFsim like any other model in the suite, and
#          local_fcn_rescan_gate_test turns the cost half into a hard ctest
#          gate by running this model against a folded-constant twin.
# Regression: #39 made a local rate that reads ANY global take a full O(N)
#          rescan after every event.  The guard answered "can this rule read
#          a moving global?" when what gates an O(N) rescan is "did that
#          global actually move?" — and for a constant `Vol` the honest
#          answer is no, forever.  RM now caches the resolved dependency
#          values and rescans only when one of them changes.
# invariant: conserved Vol = 50
# invariant: conserved Aphos = 20000
# invariant: nonneg

begin model
begin parameters
    X0    20000    # reactive:  Aphos(x) = 1, flips at kf*Vol
    I0     2000    # inert:     Aphos(x) = 0, must never fire
    kf    2.0e-4   # kf*Vol = 0.01 per reactive molecule
end parameters

begin molecule types
    V()
    A(m~0~1,p~0~1)
end molecule types

begin seed species
    V()              50
    A(m~0,p~1)       X0
    A(m~0,p~0)       I0
end seed species

begin observables
    # Referenced BARE by aflip -> system-wide count, and constant: no rule
    # creates or destroys V.
    Molecules  Vol    V()
    # Referenced applied to the tag -> evaluated at the tagged molecule,
    # 1 for the reactive half and 0 for the inert half.
    Molecules  Aphos  A(p~1)
    Molecules  Aoff   A(m~0)
    Molecules  Aon    A(m~1)
end observables

begin functions
    # Vol bare (global, = 50 throughout); Aphos(x) tagged (local, 0 or 1).
    aflip(x) = kf*Vol*Aphos(x)
end functions

begin reaction rules
    # The tag is repeated on the product so BNG2 maps the molecule through
    # the rule; without it the untouched `p` component reads as a missing
    # component on a newly created molecule.
    RA: A(m~0)%x -> A(m~1)%x    aflip(x)
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
simulate({method=>"nf",t_end=>100,n_steps=>20})
end actions
